course: dictionary
lesson: 13520
title: Impelled: pushed or urged
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Impelled» is a formal word, so you will meet it in stories and serious writing more than in everyday talk. It comes from «impel», which means to push or urge something forward, or to make someone feel they must act.
explain: «I felt impelled to speak up.» The clues are «felt» and «speak up». Try your meaning in the sentence: «I felt pushed to speak up» still makes sense, so impelled means driven by a strong feeling inside you.
explain: The same word can describe a push from outside. «The wind impelled the boat across the lake» means the wind pushed the boat forward. In both sentences, something is driving something else onward, whether it is a feeling or a force.
fact: Impel is a verb. Impelled is its past tense: «She impelled the ball» becomes «She impelled the ball yesterday» (past).
fact: Impelled can mean made to feel you must do something, driven by a strong feeling or need.
fact: Impelled can also mean pushed or driven forward by a force.
fact: «Impelled» is often used in the phrase «felt impelled to», as in «I felt impelled to speak up».
fact: In science, a force can impel an object forward, such as a kick impelling a football.
exercise: «She felt impelled to help the lost puppy.» What does impelled mean here? | Felt sleepy and tired | *Felt a strong urge to do something | Felt cold in the wind | Felt sorry for nobody
exercise: «The wind impelled the boat across the lake.» What does impelled mean here? | Made very quiet | Painted in bright colours | *Pushed or driven forward by a force | Stopped completely
exercise: Ben says, «I was impelled to tell the truth.» Which word is closest in meaning to impelled? | Tasted | *Urged | Hid | Forgot
test: «Rain impelled the crowd to run for shelter.» What does impelled suggest? | Stopped them from moving | Left them alone | *Pushed or driven them to move quickly | Made them sing loudly
test: «Mia felt impelled to apologise after she broke the vase.» What is the best meaning of impelled here? | *Felt a strong need to say sorry | Forgot her name | Felt hot | Felt bored
exam: «The engine impelled the rocket upwards.» In this sentence, impelled means | Repaired by hand | Made quiet by a force | *Driven forward or upwards by a force | Cooled down slowly
